## What I added

**1. `codx/junior/browser/scripts.py`** — the library itself (no browser dependency, fully unit-testable):

- `BrowserScriptStore(project_path)` — catalogue at `.codx/browser_scripts/index.json`, one folder per script (`<id>/script.json` + `script.<ext>` + `versions/v<N>.<ext>`), atomic writes, per-instance lock, self-healing index (`test_index_is_rebuilt_when_missing`).
- `save_script(...)` creates **or updates in place** (same `script_id`, or same title+site): archives the previous body to `versions/`, bumps `version`, keeps `uses`/`created_at`. Renaming never moves a folder (id is canonical).
- `get_script`, `find_script`, `search_scripts` (score by title/site/tags/description, then uses, then recency), `list_scripts`, `mark_used`, `stats`, `delete_script` (soft → `.trash/`).
- `normalize_site()` maps any URL to a site key (`https://www.GitHub.com/x` → `github.com`), with parent/subdomain matching.
- **Security decision:** scripts are *data*. `language="steps"` is a JSON array of `browse_action`-style steps replayed by the browser layer — there is no `eval`/`exec` of model-written Python in the API process (those recipes are written by an LLM and stored on disk). `javascript` is only meant for in-page evaluation.

**2. `codx/junior/tools/browser_script_tools.py`** — `list_browser_scripts`, `get_browser_script`, `save_browser_script`, `delete_browser_script`, plus `BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOLS` / `BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOL_NAMES` ready-made registry entries (`{tool_json, settings, tags, tool_call}`).

**3. `tests/browser/test_browser_scripts.py`** — 12 tests over the store, steps validation, versioning and soft delete.

## Two integration edits I did not touch

I could not read `tools/__init__.py` (1619 lines) or `browser.profile` verbatim in this session, so I won't risk a blind full-file rewrite. Both edits are one-liners:

In `codx/junior/tools/__init__.py`, next to the browser tool imports:

```python
from codx.junior.tools.browser_script_tools import BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOLS
```

and spread the entries into the tool registry list (`TOOLS`), e.g. `TOOLS = [ ... , *BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOLS]` (or `TOOLS.extend(BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOLS)` after the definition).

In `codx/junior/profiles/browser.profile`, append to `tools:`:

```yaml
    - list_browser_scripts
    - get_browser_script
    - save_browser_script
    - delete_browser_script
```

## Please confirm two assumptions

1. `ToolResponse(user_response=..., llm_response=...)` — I rely on `logs`/`cost` having defaults.
2. `BROWSER_SCRIPT_TOOL_SETTINGS` reuses `BROWSER_TOOL_SETTINGS` from `browser_tools.py` (same async + project settings requirements). If `ToolSettings` needs a per-tool name/scope field, set it explicitly in the entries.

`resolve_project_path(project_id, project_path)` is the single adapter point: explicit path → `CODXJuniorSettings` → env → cwd. Everything else is browser-API-free, so the next step (a `run_browser_script` that executes the steps through `BrowserManager`) only has to bind `store.get_script(id).steps` to the existing `browse_action` plumbing — say the word and I'll wire it once you point me at that call path.

